# This repository is written on Windows and runs on Linux.
#
# core.autocrlf is on here, so without this file a shell script or a systemd
# unit can reach the server with CRLF endings, and the failure is not obvious:
# a `#!/usr/bin/env bash\r` shebang reports "no such file or directory" naming
# an interpreter that plainly exists. Everything below is read by Linux, so it
# is checked out with LF wherever it is cloned.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh        text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf
Makefile    text eol=lf
*.service   text eol=lf
*.timer     text eol=lf
*.conf      text eol=lf

# Binary, so leave the bytes alone.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.db  binary

# Riot's domain verification file. It must contain the code and nothing else,
# so it is kept exactly as written: no end-of-line normalization, and nothing
# appended on checkout.
frontend/public/riot.txt -text
